 75CO    9BE(86KR,X):T1/2:XUNDL-1      2010HO12                           201008
 75CO c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2010Ho12                           
 75CO c  Phys Rev C 82, 025806 (2010)                                           
 75CO c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), August 19, 2010                       
 75CO c  2010Ho12: {+9}Be({+86}Kr,X) E=140 MeV/nucleon; fully-ionized {+86}Kr   
 75CO2c  beam, A1900 fragment separator at NSCL facility using B|r-|DE-B|r      
 75CO3c  method. After separation, the mixed beam was implanted into the        
 75CO4c  NSCL |b-counting system (BCS) consisting of stacks of Si PIN           
 75CO5c  detectors, a double-sided Si strip detector (DSSD) for implantation of 
 75CO6c  ions, and six single-sided Si strip detectors (SSSD) followed by two   
 75CO7c  Si PIN diodes. The identification of each implanted event was made     
 75CO8c  from energy loss, time-of-flight information and magnetic rigidity.    
 75CO9c  The implantation detector measured time and position of ion            
 75COAc  implantations and |b decays. Neutrons were detected with NERO detector.
 75COBc  Measured |b- and |bn-correlated events with ion implants;              
 75COCc  half-life of {+75}Co and delayed-neutron emission probability          
 75CO  L  0                             30 MS    11                             
 75CO2 L %B-N<16 (2010Ho12)                                                     
 75CO cL $ A total of 76 implants were detected, and one correlated |bn         
 75CO2cL coincidence was observed                                               
 75CO cL T$ from measurement of time sequence of decay type events correlated   
 75CO2cL with the implanted nuclei (of {+75}Co) in Si detectors (2010Ho12)      
 75CO3cL The authors used method of maximum likelihood analysis                 
 75CO4cL which required, as input parameters, values of |b-detection efficiency,
 75CO5cL background, half-lives of daughter and granddaughter nuclei and        
 75CO6cL experimental or theoretical values of %|b{+-}n of all nuclei involved  

