 75CU c  Compiled by E. Thiagalingam and B. Singh (McMaster); Jan 9, 2013       
 75CU c  {+238}U beam at E=345 MeV/nucleon provided by the RIBF accelerator     
 75CU2c  complex at RIKEN facility. Fission fragments were separated and        
 75CU3c  analyzed by BigRIPS separator, transported to focal plane of           
 75CU4c  ZeroDegree spectrometer and finally implanted in an aluminum stopper.  
 75CU5c  Particle identification was achieved by |DE-tof-B|r method.            
 75CU6c  Delayed gamma rays from microsecond isomers were detected by three     
 75CU7c  clover-type HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, isomer       
 75CU8c  half-life. Deduced levels. Comparison with previous studies.           
