 75CU    U(P,X):ISOTOPE SHIFT:XUNDL-6  2016BI08                           201609
 75CU c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2016Bi08:                          
 75CU c  Phys. Rev. C 93, 064318 (2016).                                        
 75CU c  Compiled by M.S. Basunia (LBNL), July 18, 2016                         
 75CU c  {+75}Cu isotope was produced by bombarding UC{-x} target               
 75CU2c  with 1.4 GeV proton beam at the CERN-ISOLDE facility.                  
 75CU3c  Cu isotopes were selectively ionized by the RILIS laser ion source,    
 75CU4c  accelerated to 30 keV, mass separated with the high-resolution mass    
 75CU5c  separator, and injected into the gas-filled linear Paul trap. Measured 
 75CU6c  isotope shift with respect to {+65}Cu using the collinear laser        
 75CU7c  spectroscopy setup. Studied systematics of isotope shifts on {+58-75}Cu
 75CU8c  isotopes. Compared with droplet model predictions.                     
 75CU cL E,J,T$From the Adopted Levels for {+75}Cu in the ENSDF database.       
 75CU c  The systematic uncertainty for isotope shift resulted from             
 75CU2c  uncertainties of the atomic factors M{-k} and F{-k} (2016Bi08).        
 75CU  L 0.0         5/2(-)            1.224 S   3                              
 75CU cL J$5/2- in 2016Bi08                                                     
 75CU cL $|d<r{+2}>({+65}Cu, {+75}Cu)=0.546 fm{+2} {I21} (stat) {I80} (syst).   

 75CU    BE(86KR,XG):ISOMER T:XUNDL-7  2016PE14                           201610
 75CU c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2016Pe14: Phys Rev C 94, 024319    
 75CU2c  (2016)                                                                 
 75CU c  Compiled by G. G~urdal (Millsaps College), October 1, 2016             
 75CU c  {+75}Cu was produced via fragmentation of  {+86}Kr primary beam on a   
 75CU2c  rotating 755-|mm-thick Be target at 60.4 MeV/nucleon at the Grand      
 75CU3c  Accelerateur d'Ions Lourds (GANIL) facility. The reaction products     
 75CU4c  were selected and separated in flight by the LISE2k spectrometer. Two  
 75CU5c  consecutive silicon detectors located at the focal plane of LISE2k     
 75CU6c  were used to detect the heavy ions. The identified fragments were      
 75CU7c  implanted in a rectangular foil. The |g-rays were detected using HPGe  
 75CU8c  detectors placed on both side of the implantation foil. A LEPs         
 75CU9c  detector was used to detect low-energy |g-rays. The total |g-ray       
 75CUac  detection efficiency was measured as 20% at 130 keV. The time elapsed  
 75CUbc  between the implantation of an ion and a delayed |g-ray  was measured  
 75CUcc  using TACs with 4|ms range. Measured: |DE, magnetic rigidity, tof,     
 75CUdc  E|g, I|g, |g-|g coin, isomer T{-1/2}. Comparison with Shell Model      
 75CUec  calculations.                                                          
 75CU cL E$From E|g data.                                                       
 75CU cL J$The J|p of excited states were discussed and many scenarios with     
 75CU2cL comparisons of transition strengths with shell model calculations      
 75CU3cL are given in 2016Pe14, however, no definite conclusion could be        
 75CU4cL reached. 2016Pe14 favor the scenario of (1/2-) for the 61.7-keV        
 75CU5cL level and (3/2-) for the 66.2-keV level based on the fact that         
 75CU6cL the upper isomer is almost exclusively populated directly in           
 75CU7cL the reaction.                                                          
 75CU cL J(A)$From 2009Fl03 (Phys Rev Lett 103, 142501).                        
 75CU cL T$From ion gated |g(t).                                                
 75CU cG E,RI$From 2016Pe14                                                     
 75CU cG $The authors stated that the multipolarities of |g-ray transitions     
 75CU2cG were assumed either to be pure M1 or E2. The multipolarity of the      
 75CU3cG |g-ray transitions were estimated depending on whether the             
 75CU4cG multipolarity of 61.7|g was a pure M1 or a pure E2 and from the        
 75CU5cG I{-total}, the decay pattern, the possible configuration of the        
 75CU6cG states and the comparison with the measured T{-1/2} in 2016Pe14. The   
 75CU7cG compiler did not quote the possible multipolarity scenarios. Please    
 75CU8cG see Table 1 for the possible multipolarity scenarios for each |g-ray   
 75CU9cG transition.                                                            
 75CU PN                                                                     5  
 75CU  L 0.0          5/2(-)                                                A   
 75CU  L 61.7      4  (1/2-,3/2-)       310 NS    8                             
 75CU cL T$minimal feeding from both the higher spin states of {+75}Cu and the  
 75CU2cL reaction was observed but no feeding-correction was mentioned in       
 75CU3cL 2016Pe14.                                                              
 75CU cL $Possible configuration: |pf{-5/2}~#2{++}                              
