 75CU    75CU:G FACTOR:XUNDL-9         2019IC02                           201912
 75CU c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2019Ic02:                          
 75CU2c  Nature Physics 15, 321 (2019)                                          
 75CU c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), November 28, 2019                     
 75CU c  2019Ic02: 30% {I5} spin-aligned beam of {+75}Cu was produced in a      
 75CU2c  two-step projectile fragmentation process. Secondary beam of {+76}Zn   
 75CU3c  was produced in {+9}Be({+238}U,F),E=345 MeV/nucleon using the in-flight
 75CU4c  superconducting separator BigRIPS at the RIKEN RIBF facility. The      
 75CU5c  {+76}Zn beam bombarded a secondary target producing {+75}Cu beam       
 75CU6c  through the removal of one proton from {+76}Zn. Measured E|g, g factor 
 75CU7c  of the 66.2-keV state by time-differential perturbed angular           
 75CU8c  distribution (TDPAD) measurement using Cu-metal stopper, dipole magnet,
 75CU9c  four Ge detectors, a scintillation detector and a collimator. Analyzed 
 75CUAc  angular anisotropies for the 61.7- and 66.2-keV |g rays. The g factor  
 75CUBc  was deduced from observed time-dependent anisotropy of the deexciting  
 75CUCc  |g-rays emitted from nuclei during spin precession under an external   
 75CUDc  magnetic field. Comparison with Monte Carlo Shell-model calculations.  
 75CU c  The E|g values, level energies and half-lives are from 2016Pe14:       
 75CU2c  Phys. Rev. C 94, 024319 (also 2013Pe03: Acta Phys. Pol. B44, 637, from 
 75CU3c  which these data were adopted in {+75}Cu Adopted Levels in the         
 75CU4c  ENSDF database, June 2013 update).                                     
