 75GA2c  Phys Rev C 96, 044324 (2017)                                           
 75GA c  Compiled by Y. Ichikawa (RIKEN)and F.G. Kondev (ANL); November 7, 2017 
 75GA c  {+75}Ga was produced at the ISOLDE-CERN facility from UCx target       
 75GA2c  irradiated by neutrons produced by 1.4 GeV proton beam incident on     
 75GA3c  a solid tungsten neutron converter. The Ga isotopes were ionized using 
 75GA4c  the RILIS sources and mass separated using a high-resolution mass      
 75GA5c  separator and their properties studied using the Collinear resonance   
 75GA6c  ionization spectroscopy technique. Deduced: spins, magnetic            
 75GA7c  dipole and electric quadrupole moments, and isotope shift.             
 75GA8c  Comparison with large-scale shell-model calculations using             
 75GA9c  JUN45 and GXPF1 interactions.                                          
