 75GE c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2019Zi01:                          
 75GE2c  Phys Rev C 99, 024327 (2019)                                           
 75GE c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL, MSU), May 6, 2019                           
 75GE c  2019Zi01: Negative muon beams were produced from the |mE4 and |mE1     
 75GE2c  lines of the Paul Scherrer Institute (|Y) in Switzerland. Target was   
 75GE3c  800 mg/cm{+2} Se granules (92.4% enriched in {+76}Se). |uX rays and |g 
 75GE4c  rays were detected with HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, E(|mX ray), 
 75GE5c  I(|mX ray), |g(t). Deduced muon lifetime, partial capture rates        
 75GE6c  to excited states.                                                     
 75GE cL $Muon disappearance lifeime=148.48 ns {I10} (capture+decay), from which
 75GE2cL the total muon capture rate is deduced as |l{-cap}=6.300|*10{+6} s{+-1}
 75GE3cL {I4} (2019Zi01).                                                       
