 75AS4cL cross sections used to assign separate cross sections. See details     
 75AS5cL of the fitting procedure for unresolved peaks in 2008KaZT              
 75AS cL E(U)$ 1431 group corresponds to L=1+4 doublet as in earlier            
 75AS2cL literature (although L=1 was also proposed in another study, albeit    
 75AS3cL with a poor fit to angular distribution). In 2008KaZT this group is    
 75AS4cL assumed to be dominantly L=4                                           
 75AS cL E(V)$ This group corresponds to previously known 1063+1075 doublet,    
 75AS2cL both with L=1. In 2008KaZT, it is analyzed as a single L=1 state       
 75AS cL L$ 2008KaZT relied on the assignment of L transfers                    
