 75AS c  Compiled by C.D. Nesaraja (ORNL)                                       
 75AS c  29 January, 2017                                                       
 75AS c  Experimental Setup: E({+9}Be)= 42 MeV from HI-13 tandem                
 75AS2c  facility at China Institute of Atomic Energy (CIAE). The target        
 75AS3c  was 3.1 mg/cm{+2} {+70}Zn with a Pb backing.                           
 75AS c  Detectors: Gammas were detected using |g detector array that comprised 
 75AS2c  of 8 HPGe with BGO anti-Compton suppressors, one clover HPGe detector  
 75AS3c  and one planar HPGe detector. FWHM= 2.0-3.0 keV at 1.33 MeV            
 75AS c  Measured: E|g, |g|g coin., I|g, DCO ratios                             
 75AS c  Deduced: Partial level scheme constructed from |g|g-coincidence        
 75AS2c  relationships, intensity balance and DCO ratios                        
 75AS c  Theoretical Analysis: Calculated bandhead of dipole band               
 75AS2c  using TAC-CDFT calculation with |a(P)-PK1 interaction. Experimental    
 75AS3c  excitation energies are reproduced in the calculation for the          
 75AS4c  3-quasiparticle configuration band                                     
 75AS cG $DCO ratios are for 40|' and 90|' geometry, with gates set on |DJ=2,   
 75AS2cG quadrupole transitions for all transitions except the 815.4 |g which   
 75AS3cG was gated by a dipole transition. Expected DCO values are: > 1.0 for   
 75AS3cG stretched quadrupole and < 0.8 for stretched dipoles                   
 75AS cG E$Uncertainties between 0.1 and 0.5 keV are stated in 2017Li02.        
 75AS2cG Compiler assigns uncertainties as follows 0.5 keV for I|g|< 10,        
 75AS3cG 0.3 keV for 10< I|g <50 and 0.1 keV for I|g|> 50                       
