 75SR    9BE(124XE,X):T12:XUNDL-2      2019SI33                           202004
 75SR c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2019Si33                           
 75SR c  Phys. Rev. C 100, 044311 (2019)                                        
 75SR c  Compiled by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC,BNL) March 11, 2020                   
 75SR c  {+75}Sr nuclei were produced at the RIBF-RIKEN facility                
 75SR2c  in the {+9}Be({+124}Xe,X) reaction at E=345 MeV/nucleon.               
 75SR3c  Fragments were separated in the first stage of BigRIPS                 
 75SR4c  and then identified by measuring |DE, tof and B|r using BigRIPS        
 75SR5c  and the zero-degree spectrometer. Reaction products were implanted     
 75SR6c  into the beta-counting system WAS3ABi, consisting of a double-sided    
 75SR7c  silicon-strip detector. Measured implanted ion-|b{++}-t; deduced       
 75SR8c  T{-1/2}.                                                               
 75SR  L 0.0                           81.7 MS   34                             
 75SR cL T$from 2019Si33, using |X{+2} fit to implant-|b(t) exponential         
 75SR2cL decay included contributions from the parent, daughter and             
 75SR3cL grand-daughter decays (if appropriate), as well as a constant          
 75SR4cL background.                                                            


